# Installing Web Server on EC2

## Simple Step-by-Step Guide

Follow these steps in order. Run one command at a time.

---

## Step 1 — Launch an Ubuntu EC2 Instance

Create an Ubuntu EC2 instance from the AWS Console.

In the Security Group, allow:

- SSH — Port 22
- HTTP — Port 80

---

## Step 2 — Connect to the EC2 Server

Connect to the instance using SSH or EC2 Instance Connect.

---

## Step 3 — Switch to Root User

Run:

```bash
sudo -i
```

---

## Step 4 — Update the Server

Run:

```bash
apt update -y
```

---

## Step 5 — Install Apache Web Server

Run:

```bash
apt install apache2 -y
```

---

## Step 6 — Edit the Website Home Page

Open the Apache `index.html` file:

```bash
nano /var/www/html/index.html
```

Example content:

```html
<h1>Welcome to Ayan Sayyad's Web Server</h1>
<p>Apache Web Server is running on AWS EC2.</p>
```

Save the file using:

```text
Ctrl + O
Enter
Ctrl + X
```

---

## Step 7 — Start Apache

Run:

```bash
systemctl start apache2
```

---

## Step 8 — Enable Apache After Reboot

Run:

```bash
systemctl enable apache2
```

---

## Step 9 — Check Apache Status

Run:

```bash
systemctl status apache2
```

If you see:

```text
active (running)
```

Apache is running successfully.

---

## Step 10 — Open the Website in a Browser

Copy the **Public IPv4 address** of your EC2 instance.

Open this in your browser:

```text
http://EC2-PUBLIC-IP
```

Your custom `index.html` page should appear.

---

## Important

Make sure **HTTP Port 80** is allowed in the EC2 Security Group.

Use:

```bash
apt update
```

For current Ubuntu systems, `systemctl` is preferred for managing Apache services.

After the practical, stop or terminate the EC2 instance if you no longer need it.
